1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:02,492
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,492 --> 00:00:05,147
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:06,368
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,455 --> 00:00:09,013
I've been painting houses
for thirty years.

5
00:00:09,151 --> 00:00:10,427
Up and down ladders

6
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:11,234
and on my feet

7
00:00:11,234 --> 00:00:12,547
from morning till night.

8
00:00:13,011 --> 00:00:14,012
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,012 --> 00:00:15,539
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:18,011
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:19,277
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,731 --> 00:00:21,049
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:21,049 --> 00:00:21,979
and it went away.

14
00:00:22,019 --> 00:00:23,066
This is different.

15
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:24,077
Tight.

16
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:25,033
Full.

17
00:00:25,073 --> 00:00:26,053
Like a band around

18
00:00:26,053 --> 00:00:27,474
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:27,514 --> 00:00:28,709
And for two years I've

20
00:00:28,709 --> 00:00:30,072
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:31,318
Give it time.

22
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,570
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:34,872
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:35,602
At three months,

25
00:00:35,602 --> 00:00:36,578
give it six.

26
00:00:36,624 --> 00:00:37,338
At six months,

27
00:00:37,338 --> 00:00:38,825
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,891 --> 00:00:39,565
At a year,

29
00:00:39,565 --> 00:00:41,347
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,464 --> 00:00:42,558
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,598 --> 00:00:43,794
We went down the list.

32
00:00:43,834 --> 00:00:45,290
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,519 --> 00:00:46,683
Every session,

34
00:00:46,683 --> 00:00:48,323
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,705 --> 00:00:49,860
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,417
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,483 --> 00:00:52,944
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,944 --> 00:00:54,216
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,374 --> 00:00:56,712
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,712 --> 00:00:57,836
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,836 --> 00:00:59,179
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:59,368 --> 00:01:00,972
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,012 --> 00:01:03,224
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,361 --> 00:01:05,056
And after that, a second

45
00:01:05,056 --> 00:01:06,936
operation to go back in

46
00:01:06,936 --> 00:01:08,024
and do it over.

47
00:01:08,519 --> 00:01:09,607
I said no.

48
00:01:09,897 --> 00:01:12,154
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:12,154 --> 00:01:13,237
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:13,237 --> 00:01:15,024
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:15,024 --> 00:01:17,552
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:18,977
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,977 --> 00:01:20,534
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:20,856 --> 00:01:22,245
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:22,245 --> 00:01:23,327
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:23,327 --> 00:01:25,094
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:25,094 --> 00:01:26,636
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:26,636 --> 00:01:29,021
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:30,435
Couldn't climb a ladder
without

60
00:01:30,435 --> 00:01:31,728
stopping on every rung.

61
00:01:32,223 --> 00:01:33,867
The guys on my crew
started taking

62
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:35,170
the high work for me.

63
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,350
Nobody said anything.

64
00:01:36,390 --> 00:01:37,580
They didn't have to.

65
00:01:37,871 --> 00:01:39,055
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:39,055 --> 00:01:40,904
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:40,904 --> 00:01:42,150
like getting in the truck

68
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:43,488
or up off the couch,

69
00:01:43,488 --> 00:01:44,453
into a decision.

70
00:01:44,826 --> 00:01:46,317
After a long and serious

71
00:01:46,317 --> 00:01:47,654
talk with my wife,

72
00:01:47,654 --> 00:01:49,927
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:50,075 --> 00:01:51,025
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:51,025 --> 00:01:52,532
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:52,822 --> 00:01:54,283
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:54,283 --> 00:01:56,903
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:56,969 --> 00:01:58,276
No loosening,

78
00:01:58,276 --> 00:02:00,385
no infection, nothing
wrong.

79
00:02:00,778 --> 00:02:02,014
Only this time

80
00:02:02,014 --> 00:02:03,383
there was no new number.

81
00:02:03,423 --> 00:02:05,181
Nobody said give it
another six months.

82
00:02:05,221 --> 00:02:06,819
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,050
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:09,015
lot for a while.

85
00:02:09,275 --> 00:02:10,410
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:11,763
Then explain this.

87
00:02:11,808 --> 00:02:14,320
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:15,827
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:15,934 --> 00:02:17,829
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,825
Everyone in the house was
asleep

91
00:02:19,825 --> 00:02:21,510
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

92
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:22,624
with my leg up,

93
00:02:22,624 --> 00:02:24,350
trying to find any angle

94
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:25,820
where it didn't feel like
something

95
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,270
was wrapped around my knee

96
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:28,164
and tightening.

97
00:02:28,721 --> 00:02:29,374
I had a house

98
00:02:29,374 --> 00:02:30,534
to start at seven.

99
00:02:30,845 --> 00:02:32,873
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

100
00:02:32,949 --> 00:02:34,609
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

101
00:02:35,237 --> 00:02:36,227
And I just thought,

102
00:02:36,227 --> 00:02:37,801
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:37,841 --> 00:02:39,046
Thirty years with a brush

104
00:02:39,046 --> 00:02:39,934
in my hand,

105
00:02:39,934 --> 00:02:40,721
and a knee is going

106
00:02:40,721 --> 00:02:41,513
to end it?

107
00:02:41,579 --> 00:02:42,983
I can't live like this.

108
00:02:43,141 --> 00:02:44,883
So I made myself a
promise.

109
00:02:45,143 --> 00:02:45,991
I wouldn't go a day

110
00:02:45,991 --> 00:02:47,498
without looking for an
answer.

111
00:02:47,574 --> 00:02:48,871
And when I found one,

112
00:02:48,871 --> 00:02:50,035
I'd share it with everyone

113
00:02:50,035 --> 00:02:51,348
going through the same
thing.

114
00:02:51,598 --> 00:02:52,731
So I got my laptop

115
00:02:52,731 --> 00:02:53,988
out and went looking.

116
00:02:54,028 --> 00:02:55,198
Not for a product.

117
00:02:55,458 --> 00:02:56,577
For an explanation.

118
00:02:56,929 --> 00:02:58,634
Mayo Clinic forums,

119
00:02:58,634 --> 00:03:00,953
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

120
00:03:00,953 --> 00:03:02,434
doctor videos,

121
00:03:02,434 --> 00:03:03,910
medical animations.

122
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:05,559
And that's when I found a
video

123
00:03:05,559 --> 00:03:07,418
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

124
00:03:07,458 --> 00:03:10,063
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

125
00:03:10,063 --> 00:03:11,988
had been through exactly
this.

126
00:03:12,034 --> 00:03:14,424
But before I say anything
else,

127
00:03:14,424 --> 00:03:15,869
I want to be straight with
you.

128
00:03:16,272 --> 00:03:18,367
You've already had
something work fast.

129
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:19,250
The ice.

130
00:03:19,479 --> 00:03:21,272
The first week of a new
pill.

131
00:03:21,501 --> 00:03:23,085
The good day after a
session.

132
00:03:23,125 --> 00:03:24,479
Then it wore off.

133
00:03:24,810 --> 00:03:27,328
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

134
00:03:27,608 --> 00:03:29,422
Fast relief isn't relief.

135
00:03:29,804 --> 00:03:30,892
It's a preview.

136
00:03:31,101 --> 00:03:32,490
So I'm not going to tell

137
00:03:32,490 --> 00:03:33,686
you this works fast.

138
00:03:33,726 --> 00:03:34,436
It doesn't.

139
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:36,494
But if you're willing to
be patient,

140
00:03:36,494 --> 00:03:37,546
and to look at what's
going

141
00:03:37,546 --> 00:03:39,026
on around your new knee

142
00:03:39,026 --> 00:03:40,467
instead of inside it,
there

143
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,474
is a real reason it still
hurts.

144
00:03:42,724 --> 00:03:44,445
And something you can do
about it.

145
00:03:44,644 --> 00:03:45,777
Let me explain what he
said,

146
00:03:45,777 --> 00:03:47,891
because this is what
changed

147
00:03:47,891 --> 00:03:49,030
everything for me.

148
00:03:49,168 --> 00:03:51,012
He started with the
basics.

149
00:03:51,149 --> 00:03:52,773
A knee replacement takes
out

150
00:03:52,773 --> 00:03:54,468
the worn joint surfaces

151
00:03:54,468 --> 00:03:56,318
and puts in metal and
plastic.

152
00:03:56,358 --> 00:03:58,053
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

153
00:03:58,053 --> 00:03:59,631
you had before the
operation.

154
00:03:59,749 --> 00:04:01,245
That part I already knew.

155
00:04:01,352 --> 00:04:02,884
But then he explained
something

156
00:04:02,884 --> 00:04:04,411
nobody had ever told me.

157
00:04:04,487 --> 00:04:05,304
He said,

158
00:04:05,304 --> 00:04:06,673
think about a swollen foot

159
00:04:06,673 --> 00:04:07,924
inside a shoe.

160
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:09,344
The shoe didn't shrink.

161
00:04:09,502 --> 00:04:11,626
Your foot is taking up
more room,

162
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,873
so everything feels
cramped

163
00:04:13,873 --> 00:04:15,696
and tight and squeezed.

164
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,182
Your new knee sits

165
00:04:17,182 --> 00:04:18,714
in a limited space with
living

166
00:04:18,714 --> 00:04:20,517
tissue packed all around
it.

167
00:04:20,808 --> 00:04:22,656
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

168
00:04:22,656 --> 00:04:24,449
had to work through that
tissue.

169
00:04:24,709 --> 00:04:27,114
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

170
00:04:27,466 --> 00:04:29,351
At first that's normal.

171
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,255
But in some people that
swelling can

172
00:04:31,255 --> 00:04:33,998
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

173
00:04:34,187 --> 00:04:35,923
And swollen tissue takes
up more

174
00:04:35,923 --> 00:04:37,675
room than calm tissue
does.

175
00:04:37,822 --> 00:04:39,201
So when you bend,

176
00:04:39,201 --> 00:04:40,861
that tissue gets
compressed.

177
00:04:40,988 --> 00:04:41,907
When you straighten,

178
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,047
it gets pulled tight.

179
00:04:43,194 --> 00:04:44,466
That's the band.

180
00:04:44,726 --> 00:04:46,948
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

181
00:04:47,218 --> 00:04:48,035
And you start being

182
00:04:48,035 --> 00:04:49,138
the one who says,

183
00:04:49,138 --> 00:04:49,844
you go ahead.

184
00:04:49,884 --> 00:04:50,829
I'll stay here.

185
00:04:51,038 --> 00:04:52,927
And that's exactly why so
much

186
00:04:52,927 --> 00:04:55,149
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

187
00:04:55,358 --> 00:04:57,472
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

188
00:04:57,472 --> 00:04:58,417
around the knee.

189
00:04:58,534 --> 00:04:59,760
Worth doing,

190
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,664
and I'd done it.

191
00:05:01,271 --> 00:05:02,711
It does nothing about
tissue

192
00:05:02,711 --> 00:05:03,810
taking up room.

193
00:05:03,876 --> 00:05:05,101
A nerve block quiets

194
00:05:05,101 --> 00:05:06,792
the nerve carrying the
signal.

195
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,732
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

196
00:05:08,951 --> 00:05:10,299
But when that irritated
tissue

197
00:05:10,299 --> 00:05:11,811
finally calms down,

198
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:13,139
it holds less fluid,

199
00:05:13,139 --> 00:05:14,615
and it takes up less room.

200
00:05:14,824 --> 00:05:15,998
Less room taken up means

201
00:05:15,998 --> 00:05:17,597
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

202
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:19,272
That's what takes the
pressure off.

203
00:05:19,563 --> 00:05:21,166
After two years of this,

204
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:22,612
it finally made sense.

205
00:05:22,902 --> 00:05:24,854
The problem was never the
new knee.

206
00:05:24,894 --> 00:05:26,635
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

207
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,163
He calls it the squeeze.

208
00:05:28,203 --> 00:05:30,394
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

209
00:05:30,766 --> 00:05:32,686
I'd bought knee sleeves,

210
00:05:32,686 --> 00:05:35,199
compression braces,
creams,

211
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:36,955
half of Amazon really,

212
00:05:36,955 --> 00:05:38,405
and all any of it gave

213
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:39,494
me was an hour.

214
00:05:39,692 --> 00:05:40,632
I even looked at going

215
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:42,517
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

216
00:05:42,613 --> 00:05:44,155
But at $200 a session

217
00:05:44,155 --> 00:05:45,953
with nothing covered by
insurance,

218
00:05:45,953 --> 00:05:47,143
that was a quick no.

219
00:05:47,495 --> 00:05:48,751
Then one night I went

220
00:05:48,751 --> 00:05:49,966
back to that knee
replacement

221
00:05:49,966 --> 00:05:51,616
group and actually read
it.

222
00:05:51,917 --> 00:05:53,347
Thousands of people,

223
00:05:53,347 --> 00:05:55,052
years out from surgery,

224
00:05:55,052 --> 00:05:58,147
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

225
00:05:58,147 --> 00:05:59,531
nobody could explain.

226
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,844
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

227
00:06:01,844 --> 00:06:03,943
the same thing kept coming
up.

228
00:06:04,162 --> 00:06:05,613
This one device,

229
00:06:05,613 --> 00:06:06,767
and people saying

230
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:07,584
it was the first thing

231
00:06:07,584 --> 00:06:08,662
that made a difference.

232
00:06:08,922 --> 00:06:10,586
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

233
00:06:10,586 --> 00:06:11,465
alright, here it comes,

234
00:06:11,465 --> 00:06:12,435
he's selling me something,

235
00:06:12,435 --> 00:06:14,299
let me shut that down
right now.

236
00:06:14,477 --> 00:06:16,091
I'm only here because I
made myself

237
00:06:16,091 --> 00:06:18,195
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

238
00:06:18,195 --> 00:06:19,165
that if I ever found

239
00:06:19,165 --> 00:06:20,350
something that helped,

240
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,372
I'd say so.

241
00:06:21,412 --> 00:06:22,811
It's called the KenRelief
Red

242
00:06:22,811 --> 00:06:24,236
Light Therapy Wrap.

243
00:06:24,435 --> 00:06:26,177
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

244
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:28,255
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

245
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:30,333
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

246
00:06:30,706 --> 00:06:32,207
But I went to their
website anyway,

247
00:06:32,207 --> 00:06:33,188
just to see what all

248
00:06:33,188 --> 00:06:34,296
the fuss was about.

249
00:06:34,771 --> 00:06:37,426
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

250
00:06:37,426 --> 00:06:39,693
charge $200 a session

251
00:06:39,693 --> 00:06:41,133
for, off machines

252
00:06:41,133 --> 00:06:43,452
that cost fifty thousand
dollars,

253
00:06:43,452 --> 00:06:44,483
in a wrap you plug

254
00:06:44,483 --> 00:06:45,837
into the wall at home.

255
00:06:46,076 --> 00:06:48,012
Two hundred and forty
lights.

256
00:06:48,098 --> 00:06:50,498
Red at 660 nanometers

257
00:06:50,498 --> 00:06:53,174
and near-infrared at 850,

258
00:06:53,174 --> 00:06:55,345
run together for the
strongest effect.

259
00:06:55,523 --> 00:06:57,245
Four strength levels.

260
00:06:57,566 --> 00:06:59,461
A five to thirty minute
timer.

261
00:06:59,945 --> 00:07:01,488
Then I saw the guarantee.

262
00:07:01,528 --> 00:07:02,790
Ninety days.

263
00:07:02,887 --> 00:07:04,705
Results or your money
back,

264
00:07:04,705 --> 00:07:07,023
no questions, no store
credit,

265
00:07:07,023 --> 00:07:08,540
and you don't even send it
back.

266
00:07:08,892 --> 00:07:11,118
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

267
00:07:11,118 --> 00:07:12,666
days to change my mind.

268
00:07:12,814 --> 00:07:14,192
There wasn't much to lose,

269
00:07:14,192 --> 00:07:15,352
so I ordered it.

270
00:07:15,438 --> 00:07:16,680
Two of them, actually.

271
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:18,645
Only the right knee was
replaced,

272
00:07:18,645 --> 00:07:20,565
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

273
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,103
and I'd done it for two
years.

274
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:24,227
The left one was carrying
the difference.

275
00:07:24,283 --> 00:07:25,263
When it came,

276
00:07:25,263 --> 00:07:27,265
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

277
00:07:27,265 --> 00:07:28,205
because I'd been let down

278
00:07:28,205 --> 00:07:29,916
too many times to get
excited.

279
00:07:30,155 --> 00:07:32,009
What I felt was warmth.

280
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,236
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

281
00:07:34,373 --> 00:07:36,109
More like it was coming
from inside

282
00:07:36,109 --> 00:07:37,994
the knee and spreading
around it.

283
00:07:38,183 --> 00:07:39,189
And that was it.

284
00:07:39,235 --> 00:07:40,792
That was the whole
experience.

285
00:07:40,879 --> 00:07:42,074
When I took it off,

286
00:07:42,074 --> 00:07:43,064
I'll be honest,

287
00:07:43,064 --> 00:07:44,735
nothing dramatic had
happened.

288
00:07:44,984 --> 00:07:46,537
And after what that video
said,

289
00:07:46,537 --> 00:07:48,544
that's exactly what I
expected.

290
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:49,662
What was different

291
00:07:49,662 --> 00:07:50,765
was that for the first

292
00:07:50,765 --> 00:07:52,236
time in two years

293
00:07:52,236 --> 00:07:54,084
I'd done something for my
knee

294
00:07:54,084 --> 00:07:55,203
instead of to it.

295
00:07:55,555 --> 00:07:56,423
Twenty minutes,

296
00:07:56,423 --> 00:07:57,465
in my own chair,

297
00:07:57,465 --> 00:07:58,379
after work.

298
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:00,616
No drive, no copay.

299
00:08:00,937 --> 00:08:02,495
They say twenty minutes.

300
00:08:02,704 --> 00:08:03,572
I did thirty,

301
00:08:03,572 --> 00:08:04,706
twice a day,

302
00:08:04,706 --> 00:08:06,611
lowest setting that first
week.

303
00:08:06,677 --> 00:08:08,138
I put it on the calendar.

304
00:08:08,178 --> 00:08:09,250
The first week,

305
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:10,047
I couldn't have told

306
00:08:10,047 --> 00:08:11,564
you if anything was
happening.

307
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,600
I tried not to get

308
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,545
my hopes up.

309
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:14,582
I'd had things help

310
00:08:14,582 --> 00:08:16,068
for a week and then stop.

311
00:08:16,226 --> 00:08:17,952
But somewhere in the
second week

312
00:08:17,952 --> 00:08:18,983
I noticed I'd come down

313
00:08:18,983 --> 00:08:20,745
the stairs without holding
the rail.

314
00:08:21,087 --> 00:08:22,451
I hadn't decided to.

315
00:08:22,507 --> 00:08:23,977
I just did it, then
stopped

316
00:08:23,977 --> 00:08:26,005
halfway down because I
realized.

317
00:08:26,163 --> 00:08:27,123
By the end of the fourth

318
00:08:27,123 --> 00:08:28,103
week I'd slept through

319
00:08:28,103 --> 00:08:29,672
the night four times
running.

320
00:08:30,064 --> 00:08:31,443
I stood at the counter and
finished

321
00:08:31,443 --> 00:08:33,614
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

322
00:08:33,884 --> 00:08:35,447
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:35,487 --> 00:08:36,407
All of it was gone

324
00:08:36,407 --> 00:08:37,556
for two years.

325
00:08:37,744 --> 00:08:39,287
A few weeks later my wife
asked

326
00:08:39,287 --> 00:08:40,175
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:40,175 --> 00:08:41,937
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:42,116 --> 00:08:43,035
And for the first time

329
00:08:43,035 --> 00:08:43,780
in two years,

330
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:44,991
I said yes.

331
00:08:45,261 --> 00:08:47,273
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:47,273 --> 00:08:48,617
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:48,805 --> 00:08:50,639
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:50,684 --> 00:08:51,364
One.

335
00:08:51,563 --> 00:08:53,186
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:08:53,186 --> 00:08:56,429
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:08:56,996 --> 00:08:57,635
Two.

338
00:08:58,038 --> 00:09:00,836
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:00,836 --> 00:09:01,867
so it takes up more

340
00:09:01,867 --> 00:09:03,170
room than it should.

341
00:09:03,430 --> 00:09:04,130
Three.

342
00:09:04,176 --> 00:09:06,168
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:07,837
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:08,107 --> 00:09:09,982
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:10,252 --> 00:09:11,509
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:11,549 --> 00:09:12,423
Four.

347
00:09:12,662 --> 00:09:14,797
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:14,797 --> 00:09:17,411
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:17,411 --> 00:09:18,872
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:18,872 --> 00:09:20,103
can come down with it.

351
00:09:20,424 --> 00:09:21,752
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:21,752 --> 00:09:23,570
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:24,775
a knee replacement

354
00:09:24,775 --> 00:09:26,082
had less pain,

355
00:09:26,082 --> 00:09:28,053
less swelling and better
early

356
00:09:28,053 --> 00:09:29,754
movement than those who
weren't.

357
00:09:30,045 --> 00:09:32,945
A 2025 review said the
same,

358
00:09:32,945 --> 00:09:34,273
and was clear the evidence

359
00:09:34,273 --> 00:09:35,300
is still limited.

360
00:09:35,621 --> 00:09:36,867
I probably sound like a
broken

361
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:38,215
record to my family

362
00:09:38,215 --> 00:09:39,548
and the guys on my crew.

363
00:09:39,992 --> 00:09:41,820
But after two years of
doing everything

364
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,781
I was told and getting
nowhere,

365
00:09:43,781 --> 00:09:44,884
you have no idea what it's

366
00:09:44,884 --> 00:09:46,437
like to sleep through the
night,

367
00:09:46,437 --> 00:09:47,846
say yes to the walk,

368
00:09:47,846 --> 00:09:49,108
and get my life back.

369
00:09:49,347 --> 00:09:50,497
So take it from me.

370
00:09:50,644 --> 00:09:51,982
Don't spend another year
waiting

371
00:09:51,982 --> 00:09:52,846
for it to settle.

372
00:09:52,983 --> 00:09:54,592
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

373
00:09:54,964 --> 00:09:56,272
More than ten thousand
people

374
00:09:56,272 --> 00:09:57,446
with pain after a knee

375
00:09:57,446 --> 00:09:59,351
replacement have already
tried this.

376
00:09:59,509 --> 00:10:01,271
Some had it worse than I
did.

377
00:10:01,501 --> 00:10:03,707
You can get the KenRelief
wrap

378
00:10:03,707 --> 00:10:05,004
from their website,

379
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:06,556
with a discount link

380
00:10:06,556 --> 00:10:08,216
and ninety days to try it.

381
00:10:08,925 --> 00:10:10,835
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

382
00:10:10,835 --> 00:10:12,143
you get your money back

383
00:10:12,143 --> 00:10:13,394
and you keep the wrap.

384
00:10:13,685 --> 00:10:15,217
They only release so many

385
00:10:15,217 --> 00:10:16,427
at that price.

386
00:10:16,626 --> 00:10:17,933
If it's still there,

387
00:10:17,933 --> 00:10:18,883
get one,

388
00:10:18,883 --> 00:10:20,293
and stop the squeeze.

